## Lab OSPF Multiarea: Multi-Area OSPFv2 Implementation, Router Roles (ABR), and Route Summarization

**Author:** Rafael Andrés Ramírez Benavides
**Role:** Junior Network Engineer

---

## 1. Executive Summary

A multi-area network topology was designed and implemented using **OSPFv2** to optimize Link-State Database (LSDB) size and reduce routing overhead in expanding corporate networks.

Two non-backbone areas were configured and interconnected through a core Backbone Area (Area 0):

- **Area 10** (Branch Office)
- **Area 20** (Data Center)

Route summarization was configured on the Area Border Routers (ABRs), along with interface hardening, to improve convergence time and operational efficiency across the domain.

