![End-to-end ping from PC1 to PC2](ping-exitosoOSPF-Multiarea.png)

**Key evidence:**

- Successful ICMP echo replies confirm end-to-end connectivity between the Branch LAN (Area 10, `192.168.10.0/24`) and the Data Center LAN (Area 20, `192.168.20.0/24`) across the Area 0 backbone.
- `TTL=125` confirms the traffic was routed through three Layer 3 hops (R1, R2, R3): the host starts at TTL 128 and each router decrements it by 1.
- The single timeout on the first attempt is expected: the first packet triggers ARP resolution along the path. The second run shows 0% packet loss.

